fields.docComment:
Durable reviewer lifecycle. `candidate` is machine-proposed/unreviewed;
`confirmed` and `rejected` are human or exact-identifier decisions;
`superseded` preserves history after a newer mapping replaces this one.

JSON array of watchlist tag objects, each:
  { tag, issueArea?, synonyms[], relatedEntities[], riskTerms[],
    position?: 'support'|'oppose'|'monitor', priority: 'low'|'med'|'high' }

models.docComment:
LegiScan session registry — sineDie backs the dead_by_deadline status (S3);
convene/crossover/cutoff procedural-calendar fields are added progressively
in Phase 1 (M2), priority states first.

A discrete, attributable statement MeriV2 asserts about a subject. Every
claim surfaced in an artifact must carry >= 1 Evidence row (SC3.3);
unsupported claims are flagged, not emitted.

§1.3 — typed, evidence-bearing edge between two budget lines. status
'candidate' edges render dashed + labeled and are NEVER silently promoted;
acceptance is a human review action (mirrors PeProgramMatch discipline).

fields.docComment:
State Legislation Platform (Phase 0, DD5) — additive, default-preserving:
empty = federal-only (today's behavior, zero migration surprise);
non-null entries also match the state corpus for those states.

models.docComment:
The unified alert object (§6). sourceType distinguishes bill/hearing/combined;
evidence carries the source-specific proof (bill diff/section or transcript
timestamp). Shadow phase writes status='new' and never delivers.
